        details: "Following the conquest of Makkah and the deterrence at Tabuk, over seventy distinct tribal delegations journeyed to Madinah, including Tamim, Abdul-Qays, Tayy (featuring Adi ibn Hatim), and Najd. The Prophet erected tents in his mosque, dressed in his finest attire, and received each tribe with warmth, respecting their cultural idioms while instructing them in Islamic monotheism, prayer, and zakat. He sent teachers and judges back with them, uniting the entire Arabian Peninsula under a single moral code and state for the first time in recorded history.",
